#: ../../source/dev/ci-report/thresholds.rst:3
msgid "What a commit has to clear"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/dev/ci-report/thresholds.rst:5
msgid ""
"Every minimum this repository declares, taken from ``ci.yaml`` at its "
"root. It is the same table :doc:`the commit gate <../../guides/devops"
"/the-gate>` applies, and the same one ``freeports-dev ci-report --table "
"thresholds`` prints."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/dev/ci-report/thresholds.rst:9
msgid "Two columns are worth reading before the numbers:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/dev/ci-report/thresholds.rst:11
msgid ""
"**Cost** says when the figure is taken. A ``fast`` metric is measured at "
"every commit; a ``slow`` one is measured by ``make ci`` and *read* at "
"commit time from that last full run. On a production branch a slow figure"
" taken at another commit refuses the commit rather than gating it — see "
"the *Staleness* section of :doc:`../../guides/devops/suites-and-"
"verdicts`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/dev/ci-report/thresholds.rst:16
msgid ""
"**What it measures** is the one sentence that keeps a percentage from "
"being read as a different percentage. ``docs.python`` counts public "
"objects carrying a docstring; it says nothing about whether what they say"
" is true."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/dev/ci-report/thresholds.rst:22
#, python-format
msgid ""
"A minimum here is a floor this repository has *already cleared*, never an"
" aspiration. One seeded above the measured figure locks the repository "
"out at the first gated commit, and the pipeline that preceded this one is"
" the demonstration: it asked for 90 % of a documentation figure that read"
" 25.93 %. Raise one deliberately, on its own, in a commit that says so."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/dev/ci-report/thresholds.rst:30
msgid "**What a commit here has to clear**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/dev/ci-report/thresholds.rst:32
msgid ""
"Every minimum this repository declares, what it is a minimum *of*, and "
"whether it is measured at every commit or read from the last full run."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/dev/ci-report/thresholds.rst:34
msgid ""
"12 metrics, 12 gated: 5 pass, 1 not measured, 6 measured at another "
"commit; branch dev → dev (thresholds are reported, not enforced); ci-"
"check: inconclusive"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/dev/ci-report/thresholds.rst:36
msgid ""
"*Generated by `freeports-dev ci-report`, and demonstrative: it shows what"
" one run measured on one machine, not that the software is correct. To be"
" sure of any line, re-run the command that measures it and `freeports-dev"
" ci-check` yourself.* :ref:`What is gated here, and what refuses: the "
"commit gate <commit-gate>`."
msgstr ""

